{
  "note": "v0.18.93 (contract.json#autoArrive): the waiting clock with the driver driving away and back. Times are seconds after Arrived (arrivedAt = 0); waitFromSeconds is when the free wait starts (a booked ride reached early: its pickup time). events: a counting fix at `meters` from the pickup, the driver's tap on Arrived, board (Start), or the driver's no-show. expect: freeUntil / noShowAt (seconds, after the moves), pausedSeconds, pauseCount, awayAtEnd, chargedSeconds at board and the waiting line (chargedSeconds / 60 × perMin, half-up), or the no-show answer of the last no_show event.",
  "stopsNote": "v0.18.108 (contract.json#autoArrive.stops, job C9b): the wait at ONE middle stop. Times are seconds after the stop arrival (arrivedAt = 0). events: a counting fix at `meters` from the stop (one event stands for a confirmed pair), the driver's back tap at `meters`, leave, or complete. expect: pausedSeconds, pauseCount, awayAtEnd, waitedSeconds = (min(end, away.since) − arrivedAt) − pausedSeconds, chargedSeconds = max(0, waited − stopFreeWaitMin × 60), the answers of the taps (ok, not_at_stop, stop_already_arrived), and the stop line (chargedSeconds / 60 × stopWaitPerMin, half-up). firstTap (v0.18.108 round 2, S1 / S2): the first stop tap's position check, positionMaxAgeSeconds 60, 300 m; sent = the location sent with the tap, stored = the server's latest stored fix (meters to the stop, age in seconds); new apps (X-Contract-Version ≥ 0.18.108): a fresh sent location, else the fresh stored fix, else position_stale (one existed) or not_at_stop (none); older apps / no header: the stored fix at any age within 300 m, none stored = ok. nextStopAuto (round 2, M1): the 2 fixes of the confirming pair, meters to the next stop and to an open earlier stop; auto only when both are within arriveMeters (100) of the next stop and, while the open stop is not away, both farther than arriveMeters from it (slow / gap parts of the confirm are in autoArrive.confirm and not replayed here).",
